OpenSwathRewriteToFeatureXML -- Combines featureXML and mProphet tsv to FDR filtered featureXML.
Full documentation: http://www.openms.de/doxygen/release/4.0.0/html/TOPP_OpenSwathRewriteToFeatureXML.html
Version: 1.0.0 (OpenMS core 4.0.0, revision 4fdec46)
To cite OpenMS:
 + Pfeuffer, J., Bielow, C., Wein, S. et al.. OpenMS 3 enables reproducible analysis of large-scale mass spectrometry data. Nat Methods (2024). doi:10.1038/s41592-024-02197-7.

Usage:
  OpenSwathRewriteToFeatureXML <options>

Options (mandatory options marked with '*'):
  -csv <file>           MProphet tsv output file: "all_peakgroups.xls" (valid formats: 'csv')
  -featureXML <file>*   Input featureXML file (valid formats: 'featureXML')
  -out <file>*          Output featureXML file (valid formats: 'featureXML')
  -FDR_cutoff <double>  FDR cutoff (e.g. to remove all features with a an m_score above 0.05 use 0.05 here) (default: '-1.0')
                        
Common TOPP options:
  -ini <file>           Use the given TOPP INI file
  -threads <n>          Sets the number of threads allowed to be used by the TOPP tool (0 = all available cores) (default: '1')
  -write_ini <file>     Writes the default configuration file
  --help                Shows options
  --helphelp            Shows all options (including advanced)

